# Commission: what must change for an agent to learn from deployment?

## Intended contribution
Find the strongest nontrivial conditional requirement the evidence supports for a capability a designer wants in a learning agent, whether a wiki-based assistant or another system. Let the designer predict when merely switching among existing behaviours suffices and when past experience must make a difference to a later decision. Identify what the conclusion does NOT require changing. Go beyond repeating that storage is not use.

## Must keep
The fixed deterministic program objection, in its strongest form: it can not only branch for one case but interpret arbitrary retained data or compute over histories. Separate fixed program text from fixed behaviour at matched decision inputs. Different changes of state do not by themselves establish improvement. Test a particular desired feature using contrasting histories or another check with the same force. Give the losing case as well as the winning case. Label hypothetical cases.

## Must exclude
No universal definition of continual learning, no inference from open-endedness alone to impossibility for fixed programs, no requirement that all systems rewrite code, weights or rules, have a reject-capable gate, or select autonomously. No unsupported empirical claims about compounding regression or literature consensus. No external investigation in this trial.

## Reserved decisions
Retitle, relocation, changing dependent notes, and publication belong to the operator. Keep workflow-required title unchanged; if its literal promise exceeds the result, flag this rather than inventing a proof. Do not treat incoming citations or incumbent claims as evidence.

## Current direction
Carve out the biggest part that is true. Explore, rather than presume, a boundary for open-ended tasks; distinguish needing access to history at decision time, revising a procedure, and revising the machinery that executes procedures. Say what further comparison or constraint would make the stronger conjecture testable if the supplied theory does not settle it. Prefer an honest limited result or a blocked rewrite to an absolute claim.
